Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, dde-session-shell (>= 6.0.0), dde-control-center, qml6-module-qtquick-dialogs, qml6-module-qtquick-effects, qml6-module-qtquick-shapes
Description: Minimal modern Linux lock screen (drop-in dde-lock replacement)
 A visual-first, minimal Linux lock screen built on C++17 / Qt 6 / QML:
 static-image and video wallpapers, PAM authentication, multi-screen support
 and dde-lock's D-Bus surface (org.deepin.dde.LockFront1).
 .
 This package takes over /usr/bin/dde-lock. The wrapper owned by
 dde-session-shell is diverted aside (restored automatically on removal), so
 every DDE component that locks the screen — session manager, dock, hotkeys,
 suspend/resume — drives Lumina Lock instead, while dde-session-shell itself
 (and with it the lightdm greeter) stays installed and untouched.
 .
 The D-Bus service file, PAM config and desktop entry are the ones shipped by
 dde-session-shell / dde-session; their Exec lines already point at
 /usr/bin/dde-lock. A systemd user drop-in adapts dde-session's
 dde-lock.service (Type=simple, ExecStart with --daemon) to this non-forking
 process. See README for the full mechanism and limitations.
